/E (The Peaks Detection is a time-domain technique used to identify the specific moments when the heart ejects blood into the peripheral vessels, known as systolic peaks. In a PPG signal, these are the local maxima of the waveform. It tracks the actual shape of the pulse wave. It is highly sensitive to noise.)
/Pg 16 0 R
